  "term": "Norpramin",
  "definition": "Norpramin is desipramine hydrochloride, a tricyclic antidepressant. It acts in the central nervous system by slowing the reuptake of norepinephrine and serotonin, leaving more of these neurotransmitters available between nerve cells and extending their effects.",
